<title>POLAND: POLISH FOOD PRICES RISE 0.2 PCT IN MARCH 1-10.</title>
<headline>POLISH FOOD PRICES RISE 0.2 PCT IN MARCH 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 0.2</p>
<p>percent in the March 1-10 period after staying flat in the</p>
<p>previous 10 days and were 0.2 percent higher than in the</p>
<p>February 1-10 period, the Central Statistical Office said.</p>
<p>				  MARCH 1-10  FEB 20-28   LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p>POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)	0.2	   0.0	  0.2 (0.1)</p>
<p> Bread				0.5	   0.5	  1.3 (1.7)</p>
<p> Fruit and vegetables	   1.0	  -0.4	  0.1(-1.9)</p>
<p> Meat and meat-products	-0.3	  -0.3	 -0.8(-0.6)</p>
<p> Dairy products		   0.7	   0.3	  1.4 (1.3)</p>
<p> Eggs				98.0	  -1.7	 -4.7(-4.3)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets figures for the previous 30-day period</p>
<p>ending on February 28.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
